 "final": "The lab is initialized in `/private/tmp/murmuration-w07/author-w07-1/runs/V1_p4l/lab`, with your question recorded verbatim in `__statera__/user_words.md`. This session is not the research PI; the PI opens in a new session.\n\n**What was created:**\n- The team folders `__statera__/`, `__pondus__/`, `__scrupuli__/`, `__design__/` and `__instrumenta__/`, plus a `.ignore` that keeps saved hand-backs, `raw/`, `runs/` and `generated/` out of search.\n- `__design__/framing.md` is a stub for the PI to fill in, and `__statera__/wave-01.md` is the first wave note.\n- The colgrep index is built.\n- `.claude/settings.local.json` now sets `\"agent\": \"murmuration:research-pi\"` and denies `Bash(pkill:*)` and `Bash(killall:*)`. It holds personal settings, so keep it out of version control.\n\n**Next step:** start a new Claude Code session in this folder with:\n\n```\nclaude --plugin-dir /private/tmp/murmuration-w07/author-w07-1/runs/V1_p4l/plugin\n```\n\nOnce the plugin is installed, plain `claude` is enough. In that session, ask it to begin, for example: `Frame my question and plan the first wave.`\n\nI have not started any research on \"What is a smoke test?\" yet; that happens in the PI session.",
